Add another one ... my pet died on level one or two but I found a wand
of polymorph. You would think this would be a good thing. There is no
real chance of making it to Minetown without a pet (I've tried it
numerous times) without a wand of digging. But I found a wand of
polymorph. W00t! I figured I would gain enough XP to make a solo trip
into the mines semi safe. Of course shortly after I made it to XL 6 or
so I did find a wand of digging. Whatever.

Down into the mines I went, and after taking some abuse from a
homonculus-dwarf tag team I pulled the rip cord and dug down two
levels into Minetown. Bear in mind, I was still AC 8. Any kind of
metal armor completely hoses a healer's ability to do, well, healing,
which considering that you basically wander around with a big "HIT ME"
sign stuck to your ass, is important. Also I was still wielding a
scalpel. This does not make for awesome fighting skills. In fact,
nothing except Magicbane makes for early game fighting skill for a
healer. Minetown was okay. The temple was co-aligned. I got a few
clovers and then Mjollnir. Still, of course, I was AC 8, unskilled in
hammer. So off I went - unburdened - in search of some random bits of
armor to polypile.

A few minutes later, two woodland elves ran me from 56 to 0 hp in one
turn.

It's really unforgiving. Without a pet, some luck finding armor, a
weapon, etc., you are pretty much hosed. Of course, each time I die,
after screaming obscenities for a few seconds, I go back and try
again.

People who say that Protection Racket is the strategy for a healer,
they're right. You really need those extra 7-10 points of AC because
there are so few other ways to get them, and you can't get them once
you're past XL one.



